{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1486","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C1. Guessing the Greatest (easy version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only difference between the easy and the hard version is the limit to the number of queries"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers. In one query you can ask the position of the second maximum element in a subsegment $$$a[l..r]$$$. Find the position of the maximum element in the array in no more than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"40"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A subsegment $$$a[l..r]$$$ is all the elements $$$a_l, a_{l + 1}, ..., a_r$$$. After asking this subsegment you will be given the position of the second maximum from this subsegment "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in the whole"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ $$$(2 \\leq n \\leq 10^5)$$$ — the number of elements in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can ask queries by printing \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? $$$l$$$ $$$r$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$(1 \\leq l \\lt r \\leq n)$$$. The answer is the index of the second maximum of all elements $$$a_l, a_{l + 1}, \\ldots, a_r$$$. Array $$$a$$$ is fixed beforehand and can't be changed in time of interaction."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer by printing \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! $$$p$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$p$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the index of the maximum element in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can ask no more than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"40"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" queries. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Printing the answer doesn't count as a query"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query do not forget to output end of line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see documentation for other languages "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To make a hack, use the following test format."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line output a single integer $$$n$$$ $$$(2 \\leq n \\leq 10^5)$$$. In the second line output a permutation of $$$n$$$ integers $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. The position of $$$n$$$ in the permutation is the position of the maximum"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n\n3\n\n4\n\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 1 5\n\n? 4 5\n\n! 1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the sample suppose $$$a$$$ is $$$[5, 1, 4, 2, 3]$$$. So after asking the $$$[1..5]$$$ subsegment $$$4$$$ is second to max value, and it's position is $$$3$$$. After asking the $$$[4..5]$$$ subsegment $$$2$$$ is second to max value and it's position in the whole array is $$$4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that there are other arrays $$$a$$$ that would produce the same interaction, and the answer for them might be different. Example output is given in purpose of understanding the interaction."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C1","problemCode":"1486C1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1486/problem/C1"}